# BQ2597x charge pump / OTG boost, built standalone for the 6.6 v2 stack.
#
# The op6893 needs this chip for one thing: it is what produces OTG VBUS (see
# the 4.19 capture -- "oplus_bq2597x_otg_en ok" right after "typec vbus_on").
# On 6.6 the charging stack is CONFIG_OPLUS_CHG_V2, and the charger Makefile
# only descends into v1/ when v2 is off, so this driver was never built.
#
# oplus_bq2597x.c here is a copy of the v1 tree's copy (itself byte-identical
# to the 4.19 original); the only edits are documented in place.  Re-diff
# against v1/charger_ic/oplus_bq2597x.c to see them.
#
# Header search: V1 for the v2-side headers, V1/v1 for the ones only v1 ships
# (oplus_chg_symbol.h is a symlink into v1/ that does not resolve from here).
# The include paths are passed as KCFLAGS, not ccflags-y: build_module_dir.sh
# overwrites NOSTDINC_FLAGS on the make command line and a command-line
# assignment beats anything ccflags-y would contribute.
#
# No v1 .c is compiled.  oplus_vooc_init_cp() is the single v1 symbol the
# driver needs and it is a one-line setter, stubbed in bq2597x_glue.c rather
# than pulling in v1/oplus_vooc.c and its vooc state machine, which this board
# does not run.  If another symbol turns out to be needed, add an explicit
# stub to bq2597x_glue.c -- do not add a v1 object.

obj-m += bq2597x-charger.o

bq2597x-charger-y := bq2597x_drv.o bq2597x_glue.o
